{"title":"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> lies on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> lies on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be points on segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f0bd1bf44e9dd29cf5383c208c802b0dccb4920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99f9f70325371de6deea41a42eb2dccde9c8802.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, respectively, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> be a point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df5aab0f247435c8ae3d835c01f07f55317108b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> lies strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c2088533220ac56d8b222b39441370456a0dee63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PP_1C=\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" />. Similarly, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> be the point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e1f35a60641554975b9b177da663a2a3a74196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QA_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> lies strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/6/ef69b2da5c4dfa595fa60da21644702e6f367cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CQ_1Q=\\angle CBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Prove that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1ad3985e66f7bc1c87d77accfc3975ebc3598fdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q,P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> are concyclic.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2019_IMO_2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1c/2019_IMO_2.png/420px-2019_IMO_2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"420\" height=\"322\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1c/2019_IMO_2.png/630px-2019_IMO_2.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1c/2019_IMO_2.png/840px-2019_IMO_2.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2019_IMO_2a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/2019_IMO_2a.png/420px-2019_IMO_2a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"420\" height=\"308\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/2019_IMO_2a.png/630px-2019_IMO_2a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/2019_IMO_2a.png/840px-2019_IMO_2a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>The essence of the proof is to build a circle through the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4ab0a7aa15e649254b9200f501801dc2f8024c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P, Q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> and two additional points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/286019547a4af151ed79013481ce202438e89c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> then we prove that the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> lie on the same circle.\n</p><p>We assume that the intersection point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bf1515283dbd146b76682d75b2ebb84d8a0214f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> lies on the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8ed0c80fcab85b950203b5ad540a99bafe1a4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA_1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> If it lies on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f66250786df748f8273cd4c5ecae751ece84a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> then the proof is the same, but some angles will be replaced with additional ones up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Let the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/71145755882ef0f1e12d10935523847f1692373e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the points of intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bf1515283dbd146b76682d75b2ebb84d8a0214f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c29d50bec2245828e35e574a179210c7992b2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAP = \\delta.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d2b351cfcacfe9c0de2894245f810f07d37af32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PQ||AB \\implies \\angle QPA_0 = \\delta.\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac935c67cdb65659b28e228169785d43a11c8c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAP = \\angle BB_0A_0 = \\delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"17\" /> since they intersept the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27b528ac0c517e73d4491cb3a61d9da78e5c0fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2b196e9b7e57d1ec99f6534c581ea9759d2170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/baccc5cfcc1ef3827f436fcf9a36a896398524b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QPA_0 = \\angle QB_0A_0 \\implies QPB_0A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"278\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic (in circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />)\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d092e65d5ef7aa163450b4e275e25f54dd7bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = \\alpha, \\angle AA_0B_0 = \\varphi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cf4dbd774844578a81ed922d7b1f5f2b087714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PP_1C = \\alpha, \\angle BB_0C = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> since they intersept the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de82b5de37f029271b42d807a7a35ac5a7e8e7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d3509891c0152ca02cc9a195d5c6f57877421a92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_0P_1CB_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" /> is cyclic.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/0/280e40f55d679981b5abedb3ffaa5f03a1441f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB_0 = \\angle AA_0B_0 =  \\varphi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" /> (they intersept the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e27677334b6bf3e99ad57044c09b8772295dc109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0B_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> of the circle  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b12fdf5c11c84218fd54e248f711bb5f089325cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Omega).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd0de15f4cbeb454eb02ed3e8dcff99daf9a263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B_1CB_0 = \\varphi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b19352190d3e092c0c95d3cfc07b705b0cf161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B_1P_1B_0 = \\angle B_1CB_0 =  \\varphi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"18\" /> (since they intersept the arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c5e22d646731d03ebb5f73c000000ca57f7fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1B_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> of the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f323ff923898bee08edeeddac48d320824ac7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_0P_1CB_1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d9f4d1ffab0dbf5f3523f3efa005d73ea41541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PA_0B_0 = \\angle PP_1B_0 = \\varphi,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />  the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> \n</p><p>Similarly, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> lies on  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39ff5eebd99794acd0068ae889b1498d54ececd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega.$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO\" title=\"2019 IMO\">2019 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017141734\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 367/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11694/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.325      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    8.325      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17632:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017141734 and revision id 204591. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}